      "content": "Here are three alternative phrasings you can swap into the paragraph that mentions the “tough decision.” Each keeps a professional tone while adding a different flavor of metaphor or comparison:\n\n1. **Balancing scales**  \n   “Your deep expertise in cloud architecture and team leadership tipped the scales heavily in your favor, making the final choice exceptionally difficult. After weighing all of the strengths against the specific fintech experience we needed, we selected a candidate whose background aligns more directly with that niche.”\n\n2. **Cross‑road comparison**  \n   “When we compared the two final candidates, it felt like standing at a crossroads: one path highlighted your outstanding cloud‑architecture and leadership abilities, while the other led toward the deeper fintech experience we required. Ultimately, we followed the fintech‑focused route.”\n\n3. **Puzzle‑piece analogy**  \n   “Your skill set was a perfect puzzle piece for many of the challenges we face, which made the decision especially hard. In the end, we needed a piece that also contained a stronger fintech background, so we moved forward with another candidate.”\n\nFeel free to choose the one that resonates most with your style and the tone you want to convey.",
